[s2;= Tutorial: Labyrinth Game&]
[s0;b42;a42;ph Transitioning from rendering static objects to building 
a fully interactive simulation introduces new architectural challenges. 
A physics`-based game requires a stable spatial layout, reliable 
collision detection, and a clean separation between the mathematical 
simulation and the visual rendering pipeline.&]
[s5; Using the [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor^ Scul
ptor] software rasterizer, this tutorial explores the theory 
behind interactive 3D simulations before assembling a complete, 
playable Labyrinth game where the player tilts a physical board 
to guide a ball to a goal.&]
